## 5. Detector refinement, recorded honestly

The first negation detector compared the word "no" in en against "no" in es and reported
five keys: `invalid_response`, `price_unavailable`, `activated`, `identity_unavailable`,
`reservation_unconfirmed`. Reading each pair in full:

```
invalid_response     : invalid setup response       / respuesta ... no válida
price_unavailable    : price is unavailable         / ... no está disponible
activated            : owning credential unchanged   / ... no ha cambiado
identity_unavailable : identity unavailable          / identidad no disponible
reservation_unconfirmed: outcome unconfirmed         / resultado ... sin confirmar
```

English encodes these as single lexemes; Spanish renders them analytically. All five are
detector false positives, **not** translation defects, and the semantics match in every
case. The detector was changed to compare presence-of-negation with the English
adjectives included; re-run gave 0 mismatches. No finding was manufactured from it.

## 6. Cross-namespace consistency against the shipped es copy

```
$ python3 - (identical-en-string scan over every en/es catalogue pair)
cross-namespace identical EN strings: 1
SAME  wire.tunnel_setup.corrupt_intent <-> mobile.setup.corrupt_intent
      shipped ES == ours ES : True   (byte-identical)

mobile.setup.in_progress  vs shipped wire.tunnel_setup.in_progress
  shipped: La configuración del acceso telefónico ya está en curso. Comprueba su estado ...
  ours   : La configuración del acceso telefónico ya está en curso; comprueba su estado ...
  -> differs only by ; / . , the same difference the two English strings have.

"acceso telefónico"      : ours 6 uses; shipped wire.slash.mobile = "Acceso telefónico de Radient: ..."
"no des por hecho que se haya revertido" : ours billing_unconfirmed; shipped wire.tunnel_setup.unavailable (same wording)
```

Term sweep across every es catalogue (`grep -o`): `cotización` **0 hits** — "quote" has no
shipped precedent, so the namespace's rendering of quote as `precio (vigente)` could not
contradict prior copy (the sidecar itself defines quote as "fresh USD monthly activation
price"). `activar` for "enable" **is** shipped practice (cli.global_help.debug,
cli.mcp_help.add_oauth, cli.serve_help.reload, wire.memory.enabled.help, wire.errors.*), so
`quote_unread`'s "activar" is consistent with the locale — the drift is `configuring`'s
one-off "habilitando" (filed as minor, finding 2). `facturación`, `crédito`, `conector`,
`túnel`, `en la nube`, `segundo plano` — no contradicting shipped rendering found.
`cli.mobile_help.mobile` renders "Phone access" as "Acceso desde el teléfono" — a second
naming of the feature in **shipped** copy, outside this namespace; noted, not filed here.

